#: ../../technical/articles/087-modelo-workspace-read-projection.md:12
msgid "Capabilities and mechanisms"
msgstr "Capacitats i mecanismes"

#: ../../technical/articles/087-modelo-workspace-read-projection.md:14
msgid ""
"The workspace layer assembles a read-only, revision-pinned view of a "
"Modelo target in two modes: static registry inspection and grade-admitted"
" calculation snapshot. It presents schema, work review, materialization, "
"provenance, readiness, and capability assessments through typed V1 "
"results. A projection is explicitly described as having no mutation "
"authority; requests can end in one typed refusal instead of a partial "
"projection. The service code implements both successful assembly paths, "
"even though the module header still says that only the capture/assertion "
"core has landed and that the two assemblies are not built. That stale "
"statement is a concrete documentation defect, not evidence that the "
"implementations are absent. Contradictory module status and implemented "
"resolvers (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), static result "
"assembly (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), graded result "
"assembly (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/087-modelo-workspace-read-projection.md:16
msgid ""
"Target requests are converted into the existing pure work selector's "
"exact request form; no selector policy is duplicated here. The resolver "
"takes the law-selected revision and independently records optional "
"requested and stored revision assertions as `MATCHED`, `MISMATCHED`, or "
"`NOT_PRESENT`. It captures work first and derives the registry capture "
"from the resolved work coordinate, retaining the registry generation and "
"producer stamps for later freshness checks. Selector adapter and revision"
" axes (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), single work-then-"
"registry capture (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), "
"resolved target capture (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/087-modelo-workspace-read-projection.md:18
msgid ""
"Locale resolution batches requested keys against a captured catalogue. It"
" chooses the requested language when present, falls back to Spanish where"
" available, and otherwise marks the value suppressed; it retains a digest"
" of the locale data so translated labels are part of the read coordinate."
" Technical labels and canonical identities are carried separately. This "
"helps a client render schema labels without interpreting compiler objects"
" or silently treating missing localization as an empty label. Locale "
"resolution and capture (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), "
"locale summary (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), typed "
"labels and locale DTOs "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace_models.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/087-modelo-workspace-read-projection.md:20
msgid ""
"Static inspection exposes registry schema and explicit evidence "
"boundaries without pretending to have a calculation. It projects "
"casillas, bindings, formulas and parameters; walks formula expressions "
"into typed operand references; joins continuity declarations, relation "
"endpoints and export exposure to canonical IDs. Applicability is not "
"falsely attached to each casilla: its identity is modeled separately "
"because it applies at revision scope. Static casilla rows mark legal "
"grounding and constraints unavailable (`None`) where the inspection "
"source lacks those declarations, preserving the distinction from an "
"observed empty tuple. Static capability rows make only schema inspection "
"available; calculation, verification and filing-readiness are unmeasured "
"because those contributors are structurally absent. Static capability and"
" family disposition (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), "
"static capability denominator "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), formula and schema "
"relationship projection (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), "
"schema-record absence semantics "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace_models.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/087-modelo-workspace-read-projection.md:22
msgid ""
"Graded snapshots add richer casilla constraints and legal/source "
"references, scalar and repeated-row materialization, and calculation "
"provenance. Repeated values are grouped by binding only when row "
"provenance supplies an index; missing provenance is treated as a refusal "
"condition rather than flattening unrelated values. Provenance records "
"retain unlinked calculation sources with a null subject, so missing "
"attribution does not erase the source itself. Capability assessment uses "
"the captured review and lifecycle evidence: schema comes from the "
"registry; calculation is available only when the captured revision "
"belongs to the current target; verification requires the same revision in"
" review and a completed verification state; filing readiness is exposed "
"as measured only when readiness reports ready. These are evidence-"
"sensitive projections, not a claim that the underlying filings have been "
"transmitted. Graded schema records "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), materialization and row-"
"provenance requirement (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), "
"provenance rows (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), graded "
"capability rules (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/087-modelo-workspace-read-projection.md:24
msgid ""
"Both modes calculate a baseline over the target, selected revision, "
"schema identity, locale digest, contributor stamps and epochs. Facets are"
" finite pages with cursors bound to baseline, revision, schema, facet and"
" contributor epoch; a cursor whose coordinate no longer matches is "
"rejected. Static assembly supports the schema facet while work-review "
"disposition remains explicit. Graded assembly requires its work, "
"registry, calculation, bounded review and readiness contributors, checks "
"that their captured generations are still current, and returns schema, "
"materialization and provenance pages plus the exact review and readiness "
"projections. Missing target/revision inputs and stale reads become typed "
"refusals with evidence and canonical recovery actions where available. "
"Baseline ingredients and static schema records "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), facet pagination "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), static assembly "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), staleness and refusal "
"paths (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`), graded assembly "
"requirements (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/087-modelo-workspace-read-projection.md:26
msgid "Knowledge, security, and implementation assessment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/087-modelo-workspace-read-projection.md:28
msgid ""
"The public model set is strict, bounded, discriminated and frontend-"
"neutral. It separates static and graded admission, closes the allowed "
"target/facet/refusal types, bounds text and record counts, enforces "
"unique identities and facts, and checks that baselines, cursors, facets, "
"capabilities and projections refer to the same selected revision and "
"schema coordinate. `None` versus an empty collection carries a deliberate"
" evidence meaning for unmeasured legal grounding, constraints, provenance"
" subjects and readiness. These validations prevent a consumer from "
"mistaking unsupported knowledge for a clean negative answer, though they "
"do not establish correctness of producer data. Closed admission and "
"refusal vocabulary "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace_models.py`), revision "
"assertion and target invariants "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace_models.py`), baseline and "
"cursor coordinate checks "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace_models.py`), projection "
"admission checks (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace_models.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/087-modelo-workspace-read-projection.md:30
msgid ""
"`workspace_manifest.py` builds a fail-closed public-schema denominator by"
" walking Python type annotations from the registry and selector provider "
"roots. It classifies leaves as projected, derived, or backend-only, "
"records paths and destinations, rejects unsupported/unresolved shapes, "
"and imposes a 10,000-entry bound before publishing the digest. Static "
"inspection roots are kept separate from graded registry-snapshot roots. "
"Manifest captures are tied to process/domain and generation coordinates; "
"currentness is checked by regenerating the manifest digest, so a forked, "
"foreign, or superseded capture is not silently accepted. This is a useful"
" schema-drift alarm, but it fingerprints the enumerated type universe "
"rather than proving a serialized response round-trips or that every "
"runtime path emits every declared field. Manifest generation and distinct"
" roots (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace_manifest.py`), typed "
"annotation traversal and fail-closed classification "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace_manifest.py`), "
"capture/currentness model "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace_manifest.py`), current-"
"coordinate verification "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/workspace_manifest.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/087-modelo-workspace-read-projection.md:32
msgid ""
"The concrete safety boundary here is read-only projection plus exact "
"evidence coordinates, bounded DTOs, typed refusal, recovery-action "
"references, and contributor freshness checks. The assigned files do not "
"show direct filesystem or network operations, credential handling, "
"external legal validation, or mutation APIs. Those absences apply only to"
" this chunk. The assembly validates contributor currentness before "
"returning, but the files alone do not demonstrate a single atomic "
"transaction spanning all underlying repositories; the consistency "
"guarantees of the capture adapters and the race window after the last "
"check remain cross-module questions. The most notable local quality issue"
" is the stale top-level status comment. No tests were present in these "
"assigned files, so validation boundaries and stale-read behavior remain "
"unexercised in this report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/087-modelo-workspace-read-projection.md:34
msgid "Dependencies and follow-up"
msgstr "Dependències i seguiment"

#: ../../technical/articles/087-modelo-workspace-read-projection.md:36
msgid ""
"Synthesis should trace the selector, work capture, registry capture, "
"locale catalogue, calculation, review, readiness and action-catalogue "
"implementations to verify that their version stamps and typed refusals "
"mean what this assembler assumes. It should also confirm whether static "
"inspection's fixed unmeasured capabilities and the graded readiness rule "
"match product expectations, and check the manifest capture lifecycle "
"under concurrent registry updates. The manifest's typed schema walker "
"should be connected to whatever CI or contract test consumes its digest; "
"this chunk does not itself show that enforcement."
msgstr ""

